= Dawes Plan negotiation 

The Samuel Commission has concluded and the liberal politician proposes that the mining industry be 'reorganised' but rejects nationalisation. Going on to reccommend the government withdraw their subsidy that wages be cut. The Mine Owners are thrilled and immediately announce not just a 13% wage cut, but also the increase in work hours. The miners are to accept, or lose their jobs. Then to attempt to force this settlement, the mines did a lock out on their workers. The TUC is furious. There are rumours they may call for a national strike in retaliation...  

